        'Bank the tempo. Once White’s knight has gone to b3, ...a5-a4 gains time on it, and a Najdorf player reaching the same structure has spent a move getting the pawn to a6 on the way.',
        'Transpose on purpose. ...Nc6 heads for a Richter-Rauzer in which the bishop is already developed, ...e6 for a Scheveningen, ...g6 for a Dragon — the choice is made after seeing White’s sixth move rather than before it.',
